# A deterministic input exercise; the fixed value makes each run reproducible.
Let reference_value be 7.
Let guess be 0.
Let attempts be 0.

Say "Reference value exercise: enter a number from 1 to 10.".
While guess is not equal to reference_value:
    Ask "Your entry: " and save the answer as raw_guess.
    Set guess to number(raw_guess).
    Set attempts to attempts plus 1.

    If guess is less than reference_value:
        Say "The entry is below the reference value. Try again.".
    Otherwise if guess is greater than reference_value:
        Say "The entry is above the reference value. Try again.".
    End if.
End while.

Say "Correct. Confirmation completed after {attempts} entries.".
